# Freezed Cubit Pattern

Use this rule when writing or editing any cubit. All cubit states in this project use Freezed.

## When to use a union state vs a data class state

**Union** — multiple named states where available fields differ (loading, loaded, error, etc.)
**Data class** — a single shape of data that updates over time (progress, form, counter)

## File structure

```
bloc/
  my_feature_cubit/
    my_feature_cubit.dart       ← cubit class
    my_feature_state.dart       ← state class (part of cubit)
    my_feature_cubit.freezed.dart  ← generated, do not edit
```

## Union state template

**`my_feature_state.dart`**
```dart
part of 'my_feature_cubit.dart';

@freezed
abstract class MyFeatureState with _$MyFeatureState {
  const factory MyFeatureState.initial() = _Initial;
  const factory MyFeatureState.loading() = _Loading;
  const factory MyFeatureState.loaded({required MyData data}) = _Loaded;
  const factory MyFeatureState.error({required String message}) = _Error;
}
```

**`my_feature_cubit.dart`**
```dart
import 'package:bloc/bloc.dart';
import 'package:freezed_annotation/freezed_annotation.dart';

part 'my_feature_cubit.freezed.dart';
part 'my_feature_state.dart';

class MyFeatureCubit extends Cubit<MyFeatureState> {
  MyFeatureCubit() : super(const MyFeatureState.initial());

  Future<void> load() async {
    emit(const MyFeatureState.loading());
    try {
      final data = await _someRepo.fetch();
      emit(MyFeatureState.loaded(data: data));
    } catch (e) {
      emit(MyFeatureState.error(message: e.toString()));
    }
  }
}
```

## Data class state template

```dart
part of 'my_feature_cubit.dart';

@freezed
abstract class MyFeatureState with _$MyFeatureState {
  const factory MyFeatureState({
    @Default(0.0) double progress,
    @Default('') String label,
  }) = _MyFeatureState;
}
```

Initial state: `const MyFeatureState()` — all `@Default` values apply.
Update: `emit(state.copyWith(progress: 0.75))`.

## Naming conventions

| Variant purpose | Factory name |
|---|---|
| No data yet | `.initial()` |
| Async in-flight | `.loading()` |
| Success with data | `.loaded(...)` |
| Success, empty result | `.empty()` |
| Recoverable error | `.error(message: ...)` |

## Part directives — exact order in cubit file

```dart
part 'my_feature_cubit.freezed.dart';  // generated — always first
part 'my_feature_state.dart';
```

## Reading state in widgets

```dart
// Exhaustive
state.when(
  initial: () => const SizedBox.shrink(),
  loading: () => const CircularProgressIndicator(),
  loaded: (data) => MyWidget(data: data),
  error: (message) => Text(message),
)

// Partial
state.maybeWhen(
  loaded: (data) => MyWidget(data: data),
  orElse: () => const SizedBox.shrink(),
)
```

Never use `is SubclassName` checks — use `when` / `maybeWhen` / `map` / `maybeMap`.

## Adding helpers to Freezed states (private constructor trick)

```dart
@freezed
abstract class MyState with _$MyState {
  const MyState._(); // enables custom methods on the abstract class

  const factory MyState.play({required Track currentTrack}) = _Play;
  const factory MyState.pause({required Track currentTrack}) = _Pause;

  // Boolean helpers avoid is-checks in UI
  bool get isPlay => maybeMap(play: (_) => true, orElse: () => false);
  bool get isPause => maybeMap(pause: (_) => true, orElse: () => false);
}
```

Note: if all variants share a field (e.g. `currentTrack`), Freezed generates the getter automatically.

## Codegen

```sh
fvm flutter pub run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs
fvm flutter analyze
```

## Checklist

- [ ] Directory named `<feature>_cubit/`
- [ ] State: `@freezed abstract class` with `_$ClassName` mixin
- [ ] Cubit: `freezed_annotation` imported, both `part` directives (freezed first)
- [ ] Initial state is `const` constructor
- [ ] Emits use named factories (union) or `copyWith` (data class)
- [ ] Widget usages use `when` / `maybeWhen` — no `is` checks
- [ ] Codegen run, `fvm flutter analyze` passes
